  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 7.2: \"Switch point as a function of standard deviation σ for prior of N(25, σ²)\". The blue \"switches\" curve starts at 25 when σ is near 0 — coinciding with the flat orange μ = 25 reference line — rises steeply to about 70 by σ = 20, then flattens, reaching roughly 80 by σ = 40 and about 82 at σ = 100, with visible small steps in the upper range where the switch point moves by discrete amounts. The two lines meet only at the left-hand edge: the more uncertain the prior, the later the switch, but with sharply diminishing effect.",
